\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The same WebTraffic{} series through both models --- \emph  {top:} the MILLET{} baseline (423{,}707 parameters), \emph  {bottom:} ours (41{,}324). Left, the predicted class probabilities with the true class marked; right, the series coloured by each model's own interpretation (red supports the predicted class, blue argues against), with the shaded band showing where the generator put the class signal. Both models are correct, but the smaller one is far more sure of it --- $0.65$ against $0.19$ on the true class --- and puts its strongest evidence inside the marked window. The accuracy and AOPCR in the panel titles are dataset means over three seeds; the single series is an example, not evidence.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
